WEBVTT

00:03.240 --> 00:06.020
We truly owe you for what you've done.

00:06.020 --> 00:11.320
Touya, you've saved my life, as well 
as that of our prince and princess.

00:11.320 --> 00:13.740
No, you've indeed saved the empire itself.

00:13.740 --> 00:16.520
I would like to repay you somehow.

00:16.520 --> 00:18.080
Is there anything you desire?

00:18.080 --> 00:21.330
No, it was just how events played out.

00:21.330 --> 00:23.870
The results of happenstance, you know.

00:23.870 --> 00:25.290
Please don't pay it any mind.

00:25.290 --> 00:27.750
You haven't changed, Touya.

00:28.130 --> 00:32.490
I tried to grant Touya a title in Belfast,

00:32.490 --> 00:35.010
but he refused me in the same way.

00:35.010 --> 00:39.040
Though getting him to accept 
my daughter was fortuitous.

00:39.040 --> 00:40.070
Oh?

00:40.070 --> 00:43.180
Then would you accept my Lucia, as well?

00:44.950 --> 00:49.080
If you were to wed the princesses 
of both Belfast and Regulus,

00:49.080 --> 00:53.490
there could be no stronger 
symbol of both countries' alliance.

00:53.490 --> 00:55.150
Um, listen...

00:55.150 --> 00:57.110
May I speak?

00:57.110 --> 01:01.910
I, too, agree with Princess Lucia 
becoming Touya's fiancée.

01:03.160 --> 01:07.880
I've already confirmed with her 
myself that she also desires this.

01:07.880 --> 01:10.250
We also believe it would 
be a great connection

01:10.250 --> 01:12.250
to secure the relationship
 between our nations.

01:12.250 --> 01:13.300
<i>Huh?!</i>

01:13.300 --> 01:15.010
<i>What are you saying, Yumina-san?!</i>

01:15.010 --> 01:18.870
Of course, I've secured the agreement 
of the other fiancées, as well.

01:18.870 --> 01:22.040
Hey, hold on a second! 
How did it come to this?!

01:22.040 --> 01:22.680
Um—

01:22.680 --> 01:25.900
So this has already been 
discussed in such depth?

01:25.900 --> 01:27.860
Then let me ask once more.

01:27.860 --> 01:30.300
Lucia, are you sure about this?

01:30.300 --> 01:31.760
Yes, Father!

01:31.760 --> 01:34.660
I'm so happy I could faint!

01:34.660 --> 01:36.780
I've never been happier 
about anything before!

01:36.780 --> 01:40.990
I will gladly go with Touya and become his wife!

03:10.960 --> 03:15.960
Episode 5

03:10.960 --> 03:15.960
The Fifth Wife and a Newly Founded Nation

03:18.170 --> 03:21.130
I'm going to be Touya's wife!

03:22.010 --> 03:23.280
Good for you!

03:23.280 --> 03:24.490
Congratulations!

03:24.490 --> 03:26.720
I look forward to you joining us!

03:27.530 --> 03:29.200
Now this is worth celebrating.

03:29.200 --> 03:33.100
I'll have to ask you to wait until 
I'm 18 before I marry anyone.

03:33.100 --> 03:34.580
Are you still okay with it?

03:34.580 --> 03:36.570
That's no problem at all.

03:36.570 --> 03:42.450
This means Regulus and Belfast can 
form an alliance of equal standing.

03:44.330 --> 03:46.600
How does this happen every time?

03:47.160 --> 03:51.090
Your power has grown great enough to 
sway the balance of power among nations,

03:51.090 --> 03:53.350
so no one can overlook it anymore.

03:53.350 --> 03:54.970
Is that why?

03:54.970 --> 03:59.640
If someone with your power were 
to side with just a single nation,

03:59.640 --> 04:02.390
it would be nothing but 
a threat to other nations.

04:02.390 --> 04:04.260
I-I see.

04:04.260 --> 04:05.290
By the way,

04:05.290 --> 04:09.420
I think we should take this opportunity 
to officially announce Yumina

04:09.420 --> 04:13.820
and Princess Lucia's betrothals 
to the public at home and abroad.

04:14.560 --> 04:20.150
Although that means we'll need Touya 
to have fitting status of his own.

04:20.150 --> 04:22.330
<i>The issue of status still comes up here?</i>

04:22.330 --> 04:26.050
So after conferring with Emperor Regulus,

04:26.050 --> 04:31.230
we have decided to cede portions of land 
from both nations to you, Touya.

04:31.630 --> 04:32.880
What do you mean?

04:32.880 --> 04:35.280
It's not a grant, but rather a cession.

04:35.280 --> 04:40.050
You'll be founding a small nation 
on the border of Regulus and Belfast.

04:40.050 --> 04:41.820
Huh? Founding?

04:41.820 --> 04:43.170
So I'm creating a country?!

04:43.510 --> 04:49.390
And we'll have you take the crown 
as the sovereign ruler of that nation.

04:49.390 --> 04:52.270
Huh?! Me, a monarch?!

04:52.270 --> 04:54.130
Well, we're calling it a nation,

04:54.130 --> 04:56.290
but it's land without any residents.

04:56.290 --> 04:59.030
The populace would only be 
those you bring with you.

04:59.030 --> 05:01.780
However, as it would be 
an independent nation,

05:01.780 --> 05:04.830
you would be free from 
intervention by other nations,

05:04.830 --> 05:07.950
and you could set your own laws 
and do whatever you want with it.

05:08.300 --> 05:11.100
That would solve the issue of your status,

05:11.100 --> 05:14.910
and it would make you an appropriate fit 
to marry the princesses of two nations.

05:14.910 --> 05:17.430
<i>I don't think it's a bad offer,</i>

05:17.430 --> 05:19.780
<i>but it's just too much, isn't it?</i>

05:19.780 --> 05:21.530
<i>Though, now that I think about it,</i>

05:21.530 --> 05:24.380
<i>these two have already laid all 
the groundwork for it, haven't they?</i>

05:24.380 --> 05:27.750
<i>Well, I suppose it does mean 
I can obtain both status</i>

05:27.750 --> 05:31.220
<i>and some land I can do whatever I want with.</i>

05:31.220 --> 05:32.720
All right.

05:32.720 --> 05:35.540
I gratefully accept your offer.

05:36.640 --> 05:39.440
So he's finally going to be a monarch, huh?

05:39.440 --> 05:42.740
Our husband is amazing.

05:42.740 --> 05:43.680
Right?

05:43.680 --> 05:46.530
I never thought he would go this far.

05:46.530 --> 05:49.490
<i>I never thought I would, either.</i>

05:49.490 --> 05:52.130
What about the country's name?

05:52.130 --> 05:54.460
Oh... Its name, huh?

05:56.540 --> 05:58.920
Brunhild, I guess?

05:59.600 --> 06:01.380
The Duchy of Brunhild.

06:01.380 --> 06:02.730
Brunhild!

06:02.730 --> 06:04.660
In other words, the warrior maiden!

06:04.660 --> 06:05.660
Yes!

06:06.380 --> 06:10.270
So would we be moving 
to this new country, then?

06:10.270 --> 06:12.570
No, I wasn't planning on it.

06:12.570 --> 06:14.290
That might be fine for now,

06:14.290 --> 06:17.190
but I think we'll have to 
move there at some point.

06:17.190 --> 06:18.560
Huh? Why?

06:18.560 --> 06:19.970
Silly.

06:19.970 --> 06:24.460
They're going to announce your betrothal 
to both Yumina and Lucia after this, right?

06:24.460 --> 06:27.900
If you're still living here, 
it'll look like you're favoring Belfast.

06:27.900 --> 06:29.580
Oh, right.

06:29.580 --> 06:32.640
Then I guess we would have 
to go live in Brunhild, huh?

06:32.640 --> 06:34.500
What to do...

06:34.500 --> 06:37.240
Maybe I should teleport this 
whole mansion over there?

06:37.240 --> 06:42.010
I think it's a good idea to leave this mansion
as a base of operations in the capital.

06:42.010 --> 06:44.510
It can be the Duchy of Brunhild Embassy.

06:44.510 --> 06:47.520
Oh, yeah. I guess that's an option, too.

06:47.520 --> 06:51.400
Though that would mean we'd need to 
build a new place to live over there.

06:51.400 --> 06:53.010
Sorry to keep you waiting.

06:57.220 --> 06:59.560
Well? Lovely, isn't it?

06:59.560 --> 07:03.190
Um, I thought something easier 
to move around in would be best.

07:03.190 --> 07:04.830
Yeah. It looks good on you.

07:04.830 --> 07:07.280
Th-Thank you so much!

07:08.070 --> 07:09.740
Now you're one of us, Lu.

07:09.740 --> 07:13.320
Oh, right. Lu-dono, what kind of 
home would you like to live in?

07:13.320 --> 07:17.040
We were just talking about building 
a new home in the new nation.

07:17.040 --> 07:18.570
A home?

07:18.570 --> 07:22.170
Then why don't we build a castle?

07:22.170 --> 07:23.110
A castle?

07:23.110 --> 07:27.580
Yes. You will be the ruler 
of a nation, after all.

07:27.580 --> 07:28.690
That sounds great!

07:28.690 --> 07:31.390
A pretty white castle would be so lovely!

07:31.390 --> 07:33.010
A castle, huh?

07:37.810 --> 07:41.270
Uh, how do you even build one of those?

07:42.230 --> 07:44.900
I knew something like this would come up!

07:44.900 --> 07:46.010
Now is the time!

07:46.010 --> 07:49.900
The time to show you what 
the Workshop can really do!

07:52.420 --> 07:54.690
In addition to its 
mass-production capabilities,

07:54.690 --> 07:57.120
the Workshop also has automated 
customization functions!

07:57.480 --> 08:02.800
It can scan any target, customize it 
to your liking, and construct it for you!

08:02.800 --> 08:05.080
So how do we actually go about building it?

08:05.080 --> 08:08.410
We go to the site, create the parts 
according to the data,

08:08.410 --> 08:12.780
and reshape the plot of land, then teleport 
the parts in and put them together.

08:12.780 --> 08:15.130
It should be complete within three days.

08:15.130 --> 08:17.010
The Workshop is amazing.

08:17.010 --> 08:20.790
Once we have all the materials, 
we can start construction at any time.

08:20.790 --> 08:21.520
Huh?

08:21.520 --> 08:23.990
You mean raw materials for a castle?

08:23.990 --> 08:26.070
Like marble and bricks?

08:27.310 --> 08:28.940
In addition to that,

08:28.940 --> 08:30.400
there's glass and lumber,

08:30.400 --> 08:32.300
brass, iron, and other metals.

08:32.300 --> 08:37.660
Silk, cotton, hemp, and other fabrics are 
all among the necessary materials, as well.

08:37.660 --> 08:38.940
We can't get all those!

08:39.370 --> 08:44.180
Um, do all of those materials need to be new?

08:44.180 --> 08:47.330
The materials are broken down 
and then reconstructed,

08:47.330 --> 08:49.340
so using old stuff poses no issue.

08:49.340 --> 08:54.050
In that case, there should be an abandoned 
castle in the northern region of the empire.

08:54.050 --> 08:57.450
Of course! If we use a building 
that was once a castle,

08:57.450 --> 08:59.780
it'll cut way down on 
the materials we need.

08:59.780 --> 09:01.320
Nice going, Lu.

09:01.320 --> 09:02.140
Yes!

09:04.600 --> 09:06.030
Let's make the balcony big.

09:06.030 --> 09:07.290
I want a training space!

09:07.290 --> 09:09.610
An indoor martial arts area, too!

09:07.640 --> 09:09.610
We'll want a big library, too.

09:08.190 --> 09:09.610
The drawbridges should be big.

09:16.190 --> 09:18.780
You really finished it in three days...

09:18.780 --> 09:21.550
This is the power of the Workshop!

09:21.550 --> 09:23.400
It's absolutely lovely.

09:23.400 --> 09:25.120
Yes, it's wonderful!

09:25.120 --> 09:27.160
I want to see the inside of the castle!

09:27.160 --> 09:30.050
Go ahead. It's just as you all requested!

09:30.050 --> 09:32.600
I'm going to go look at the training space!

09:32.600 --> 09:34.010
Me, too!

09:34.010 --> 09:36.220
My, what a splendid castle.

09:37.050 --> 09:38.060
Leen?!

09:41.020 --> 09:42.100
My goodness.

09:42.100 --> 09:45.310
I take my eyes off you for a while, 
and you become a monarch.

09:45.310 --> 09:48.620
Talk about climbing the ladder. 
I'm more exasperated than shocked.

09:49.230 --> 09:52.690
And you're marrying the princess 
of the Regulus Empire, as well?

09:52.690 --> 09:54.940
Must be nice living a life of comfort.

09:54.940 --> 09:57.420
Did you come here just 
to make snide remarks?

09:57.890 --> 10:01.410
<i>Of course, the engagement 
announcement will come later, but...</i>

10:02.200 --> 10:05.680
<i>My position will change 
based on whether Queen Yuel</i>

10:05.680 --> 10:08.340
<i>gives birth to a boy or a girl.</i>

10:09.960 --> 10:12.890
Well, sorry to bother you while you're busy,

10:12.890 --> 10:17.550
but I ended up being sent to this 
country as Mismede's ambassador.

10:17.550 --> 10:18.340
Huh?

10:18.340 --> 10:20.820
So I'm counting on you 
to find me a place to live.

10:20.820 --> 10:22.310
Wait, hold on.

10:22.310 --> 10:25.310
I thought you were the ambassador 
posted to Belfast?

10:25.310 --> 10:27.860
I dumped all that on someone else.

10:27.860 --> 10:29.970
It seems more interesting over here.

10:29.970 --> 10:31.020
Seriously?

10:31.020 --> 10:32.940
I'm tired from my long journey,

10:32.940 --> 10:34.520
so I'll go get some rest.

10:34.520 --> 10:36.330
Go ahead.

10:36.330 --> 10:37.530
Oh, right.

10:39.530 --> 10:40.960
That should do it.

10:41.510 --> 10:43.490
Touya, what's that?

10:43.880 --> 10:46.910
It's basically a key that opens a Gate.

10:46.910 --> 10:49.640
Only those with permission 
can pass through it,

10:49.640 --> 10:51.960
and it also records who's used it recently.

10:51.960 --> 10:53.410
Wow.

10:53.410 --> 10:55.100
Let's give it a try.

10:55.100 --> 10:57.590
Renne, try touching that metal panel.

10:57.590 --> 10:58.960
Like this?

10:59.400 --> 11:01.010
Now state where you want to go.

11:01.010 --> 11:03.980
Uh... The Belfast Mansion!

11:07.190 --> 11:09.350
Well, now we know it works.

11:12.100 --> 11:13.400
Wait, where's Renne?

11:13.400 --> 11:15.200
Oh, Touya!

11:15.200 --> 11:16.860
You have a letter from the palace.

11:16.860 --> 11:19.080
From the king of Belfast?

11:21.570 --> 11:23.180
Oh, oh, oh!

11:23.180 --> 11:26.330
So you're the Mochizuki Touya 
everyone's been talking about!

11:26.330 --> 11:28.540
Touya, let me introduce you.

11:28.540 --> 11:31.420
This is the emperor of the Refreese Imperium.

11:31.420 --> 11:33.270
Rig Rick Refreese.

11:33.270 --> 11:37.100
I've heard all about you 
from the king of Belfast.

11:37.100 --> 11:38.000
Uh-huh...

11:38.000 --> 11:41.020
Let's get straight to the point.

11:41.020 --> 11:42.780
I would like to forge friendly relations

11:42.780 --> 11:45.020
between your country and 
the Refreese Imperium.

11:45.020 --> 11:49.180
Normally, I would ask you 
to marry my daughter, but...

11:49.180 --> 11:50.430
Your daughter...

11:51.880 --> 11:53.940
I'll refrain, thank you.

11:53.940 --> 11:55.370
No, I mean it!

11:55.370 --> 11:59.210
Well, her partner has 
already been decided upon!

12:00.050 --> 12:01.540
So on that note,

12:01.540 --> 12:04.030
I hear construction of 
Brunhild's castle is complete,

12:04.030 --> 12:06.740
so would you mind inviting us to visit?

12:06.740 --> 12:10.500
You mean invite the rulers 
of other nations to see me?

12:10.500 --> 12:11.320
Yes.

12:11.320 --> 12:14.710
It's a good thing to build friendly 
ties between nations, isn't it?

12:15.080 --> 12:16.920
And your real motive?

12:16.920 --> 12:19.620
Even kings want to relax and let loose!

12:19.620 --> 12:20.510
<i>Hey!</i>

12:20.890 --> 12:24.970
<i>Oh, boy. Looks like we're going to be busy.</i>

12:31.930 --> 12:33.660
Now, then.

12:33.660 --> 12:35.460
Inviting them here is fine,

12:35.460 --> 12:37.650
but where do we start preparing for them?

12:38.120 --> 12:41.910
We can have our staff at Moon Reader 
fill in for our lack of staff.

12:41.910 --> 12:44.560
Hmm, entertainment...

12:45.110 --> 12:46.910
Maybe billiards?

12:49.750 --> 12:51.390
Or bowling?

12:52.770 --> 12:54.580
Ping-pong could be good, too.

13:01.630 --> 13:05.180
I guess I'll have pinball and air hockey, too.

13:06.940 --> 13:07.980
No way!

13:08.700 --> 13:11.430
Ah, this feels great.

13:11.970 --> 13:15.320
<i>I'll need things like this for
 the kings and emperor, too.</i>

13:15.320 --> 13:16.900
Touya, Touya.

13:16.900 --> 13:18.860
This is a winning hand, right?

13:18.860 --> 13:20.470
Let me see...

13:20.470 --> 13:21.110
Wha—

13:21.110 --> 13:24.820
Big four winds, all honors, four 
concealed triplets, single wait?!

13:24.820 --> 13:25.890
Tsumo?

13:25.890 --> 13:26.930
Yeah, it is.

13:26.930 --> 13:29.710
That's a triple... no, quintuple yakuman?

13:29.710 --> 13:31.690
And you're the dealer, 
so that's 80,000 from all!

13:31.690 --> 13:32.660
Huh?!

13:32.660 --> 13:34.500
<i>Terrifying...</i>

13:34.500 --> 13:37.340
<i>I should remember to never 
join a table with Elze.</i>

13:43.560 --> 13:46.220
<i>Looks like I can leave the 
entertainment room to them.</i>

13:46.570 --> 13:48.220
<i>That just leaves security.</i>

13:48.680 --> 13:53.320
<i>I set it up so using attack magic within 
the castle would activate Paralyze,</i>

13:53.320 --> 13:57.810
<i>but I want it to be more secure 
before bringing monarchs in.</i>

13:57.810 --> 14:01.550
Oh, Master, you have a visitor.

14:01.550 --> 14:02.820
A visitor?

14:05.670 --> 14:07.620
It's been a long time.

14:07.620 --> 14:08.980
Tsubaki-san!

14:08.980 --> 14:10.950
What are you doing out here?

14:10.950 --> 14:12.200
Are you on a mission?

14:12.200 --> 14:16.550
No. I am no longer a Takeda shinobi.

14:16.550 --> 14:20.890
I have made my way here hoping 
that I might be able to serve you.

14:20.890 --> 14:21.660
Huh?

14:22.430 --> 14:24.830
The Takedas have been ended?!

14:24.830 --> 14:25.720
Yes.

14:25.720 --> 14:26.780
Even though...

14:27.290 --> 14:30.390
Even though you went to 
the trouble of saving them.

14:30.390 --> 14:33.450
The new lord neglected the populace,

14:33.450 --> 14:34.960
raised taxes,

14:34.960 --> 14:38.030
interfered with other territories, 
and did whatever he pleased.

14:39.500 --> 14:41.910
Kousaka-sama tried to admonish him,

14:41.910 --> 14:43.680
but he refused to listen.

14:43.680 --> 14:46.440
In the end, his land was taken away from him.

14:46.440 --> 14:48.700
<i>One of those foolish lords, huh?</i>

14:48.700 --> 14:51.830
So, the elite four of Takeda held a council

14:51.830 --> 14:55.790
and decided we would like to serve 
Brunhild along with the rest of our clan.

14:55.790 --> 14:57.480
I understand your situation.

14:57.890 --> 15:00.940
<i>Frankly, it would be reassuring 
to have more allies,</i>

15:00.940 --> 15:04.420
<i>and I would be grateful to have 
the elite four of Takeda here, but...</i>

15:04.420 --> 15:05.960
Wait, hold on!

15:05.960 --> 15:07.380
With the entire clan?!

15:07.380 --> 15:08.560
Yes.

15:08.560 --> 15:10.820
They are waiting outside the castle gates.

15:10.820 --> 15:13.940
Um, and how many are there, anyway?

15:13.940 --> 15:17.600
Including the children, 
there are 67 of us in total.

15:17.600 --> 15:18.580
<i>Sixty—</i>

15:18.580 --> 15:20.190
<i>That's a lot.</i>

15:20.750 --> 15:22.600
Would that be too difficult?

15:22.600 --> 15:26.480
No, I don't mind allowing them 
to live in this country,

15:26.990 --> 15:31.400
but we can't afford to hire all of them 
to work in the castle like you would.

15:31.400 --> 15:33.870
There's no need for concern there.

15:33.870 --> 15:37.450
Members of Shinobi clans 
generally have side jobs, as well.

15:37.450 --> 15:40.120
We have the skills to earn a living.

15:41.410 --> 15:43.080
<i>I guess it's fine, then.</i>

15:43.080 --> 15:44.130
Long time no see.

15:44.130 --> 15:45.450
It is!

15:51.160 --> 15:52.260
Hey, brat!

15:52.260 --> 15:55.390
Baba-san! Yamagata-san! And Naito-san, too!

15:55.390 --> 15:58.340
I'm sure you've heard the story from Tsubaki,

15:58.340 --> 15:59.870
but thanks for welcoming us.

15:59.870 --> 16:01.060
We're glad to be here.

16:01.060 --> 16:05.310
I was just looking for extra hands 
for our newly founded country.

16:05.310 --> 16:06.050
Sure thing!

16:06.050 --> 16:09.130
Leave wars and guarding the castle to us!

16:09.130 --> 16:11.530
<i>Please don't suggest something so violent.</i>

16:11.530 --> 16:14.440
To think this brat's a monarch now, huh?

16:14.440 --> 16:17.190
It might be a tiny country, 
but that's still impressive.

16:17.190 --> 16:21.140
Just make sure you don't end up 
like our lord that got fired.

16:23.070 --> 16:25.190
Oh, yeah, is Kousaka-san around?

16:25.190 --> 16:27.660
I've heard he's very skilled.

16:27.660 --> 16:28.910
He's pretty sharp.

16:28.910 --> 16:30.380
Have you not met him yet?

16:30.380 --> 16:33.090
No. But I wanted to ask him about some things.

16:34.550 --> 16:37.750
I see. So you want to attract merchants.

16:37.750 --> 16:39.720
We suddenly gained more citizens,

16:39.720 --> 16:43.890
so I figure we'll need people who conduct 
business to secure everyone's livelihoods.

16:43.890 --> 16:45.440
That's true.

16:45.440 --> 16:49.120
No city can develop without 
people passing through.

16:49.860 --> 16:52.900
The first step would be developing highways.

16:56.460 --> 16:57.640
Modeling!

17:16.430 --> 17:19.200
That completes the checkpoints, too.

17:21.970 --> 17:25.320
Now that we have streets, I want some shops.

17:25.320 --> 17:28.200
We'll need restaurants 
where travelers can rest,

17:28.200 --> 17:30.570
and places where they can obtain information.

17:30.570 --> 17:33.130
Your Highness, about the land to the south...

17:33.130 --> 17:35.050
Oh, I'll be right there!

17:36.490 --> 17:39.060
Lu-dono, it's time for lunch.

17:40.450 --> 17:41.590
Lu?

17:41.590 --> 17:43.910
Oh, I'm sorry! I didn't notice...

17:47.550 --> 17:50.350
Are you struggling with this life 
you're unaccustomed to?

17:50.350 --> 17:52.390
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

17:52.390 --> 17:54.180
Oh, no...

17:58.940 --> 18:00.780
I'm learning a lot right now,

18:00.780 --> 18:05.060
and I want to be useful to Touya, 
like all of you, as soon as I can.

18:08.600 --> 18:11.790
Touya seems like he's busy again today.

18:11.790 --> 18:15.160
Truly, being a ruler is hard work.

18:23.460 --> 18:26.270
Things are starting to take shape now.

18:26.660 --> 18:30.250
I'll be opening a new branch 
of Moon Reader here, too.

18:30.250 --> 18:31.460
Oh, Your Highness!

18:31.460 --> 18:32.350
Good afternoon!

18:32.350 --> 18:33.260
Good afternoon!

18:33.260 --> 18:34.340
Hello, good afternoon.

18:34.340 --> 18:35.890
We were quick, weren't we?

18:35.000 --> 18:36.800
Yeah. Good job.

18:36.800 --> 18:38.220
Touya!

18:38.630 --> 18:41.120
Oh, Lu. What's the matter?

18:41.520 --> 18:42.640
What's that?

18:43.010 --> 18:44.540
A lunch box.

18:44.540 --> 18:47.100
You didn't return for lunch, so...

18:47.100 --> 18:50.260
Oh, that's right. I haven't eaten yet.

18:52.620 --> 18:55.820
Um, I made it for you.

18:55.820 --> 18:56.690
You did?

18:56.690 --> 18:58.120
Yes.

18:58.120 --> 19:02.610
I heard from Yumina that 
you like dishes from Eashen,

19:02.610 --> 19:05.370
so I had Tsubaki show me how to make them.

19:05.370 --> 19:09.870
I'm sure they don't look quite right since 
it was my first time making them, but...

19:12.380 --> 19:15.760
Hey, this is good. It's hard to 
believe it was your first time.

19:15.760 --> 19:17.480
Really?!

19:17.480 --> 19:19.370
I'm glad to hear that!

19:19.830 --> 19:21.230
Is something the matter?

19:21.230 --> 19:23.850
Hmm? Oh, I was just thinking
 that you're cute.

19:23.850 --> 19:25.310
Huh?!

19:30.870 --> 19:33.890
Actually, I made dessert, too.

19:33.890 --> 19:35.230
Wow!

19:36.080 --> 19:38.940
Welcome to my entertainment room!

19:41.030 --> 19:42.490
Incredible!

19:42.490 --> 19:44.220
This is amazing!

19:46.600 --> 19:50.820
Everyone, please make yourselves 
at home and have a good time!

20:04.300 --> 20:07.510
This is truly an unbelievable sight.

20:07.970 --> 20:09.650
Just a short while ago,

20:09.650 --> 20:12.540
I would have thought it impossible 
to see all the monarchs

20:12.540 --> 20:14.230
of the western nations in one room.

20:14.750 --> 20:17.360
Now they're all playing games together.

20:17.670 --> 20:18.570
Touya!

20:18.570 --> 20:20.530
How do you play with this?

20:20.530 --> 20:21.450
Oh, that's...

20:21.450 --> 20:22.820
Have a match with us!

20:24.570 --> 20:26.640
I'll have some!

20:30.210 --> 20:31.960
It's getting late.

20:31.960 --> 20:35.730
I've prepared one last form of 
entertainment for everyone to watch,

20:35.730 --> 20:37.670
and then we'll be calling it a day.

20:38.210 --> 20:39.120
Enjoy!

20:43.280 --> 20:45.260
Those are called fireworks.

20:45.260 --> 20:46.930
You're meant to enjoy watching them.

20:46.930 --> 20:49.260
You often see them shot up
during summers in Eashen.

20:49.820 --> 20:52.980
<i>Though we're technically not 
shooting them </i>up<i> today.</i>

20:57.260 --> 20:59.980
I'm setting off the chrysanthemums!

21:06.130 --> 21:09.090
Touya, thank you so much.

21:10.190 --> 21:15.160
I mean, there's a lot I've learned 
for the first time since coming here.

21:15.160 --> 21:18.540
Things like cooking, 
as well as things about myself.

21:18.540 --> 21:23.260
Since I met you, every day 
has been so much fun.

21:23.260 --> 21:24.570
Lu...

21:26.590 --> 21:28.470
It's a little late, but here.

21:29.420 --> 21:31.370
Our marriage might still be a ways off,

21:31.370 --> 21:32.930
but it's proof of our engagement.

21:35.140 --> 21:37.190
I'm so happy.

21:37.190 --> 21:41.480
Now I can proudly call myself your fiancée.

21:43.440 --> 21:46.350
I should have given it to you sooner.

21:47.310 --> 21:48.860
Oh, it's nothing.

21:50.680 --> 21:55.180
<i>I bet we just look like 
friendly siblings right now.</i>

21:55.910 --> 21:58.300
<i>There's no need to rush, though.</i>

22:06.540 --> 22:10.850
<i>I'm sure that in time we'll look like lovers, 
and then like a married couple.</i>

22:14.270 --> 22:18.200
<i>After all, we'll be living together 
in this country for a long time.</i>
